The musician added, &#8220;I’m in his corner 100%.&#8221;

The endorsement comes amid a close race in Michigan between Dr. El-Sayed and his Republican opponent, Mike Rogers, to take over Democrat Gary Peters&#8217; seat in the Senate. A Democratic win in Michigan is crucial for Democrats as they work to flip the Senate, and recently, Michigan Rep. Haley Stevens threw everyone a curveball by rescinding her support of Dr. El-Sayed and endorsing Rogers. As a result, the state&#8217;s Democratic Party chairman Curtis Hertel announced on X that Stevens “is not a current member of the Michigan Democratic Party, nor will she be in the future.&#8221;

Springsteen has long been vocal in his political opinions, especially in recent years. He&#8217;s repeatedly spoken out against Donald Trump in particular, which has led the president to publicly take aim at the Rock & Roll Hall of Famer a number of times &#8212; not that it&#8217;s had any success in silencing the Boss.

&#8220;I do what I want to do,” Springsteen &#8212; who&#8217;s topped the Billboard 200 11 times over the course of his career &#8212; told Rolling Stone of using his recent Land of Hopes & Dreams trek as a political statement. “This was the show I wanted to make, the story I wanted to tell &#8230; I’m sure there were people, and I’ve read things where people were vehement about the content of the show. And that’s just the way the chips fall.&#8221;

